  "scope": "Two cooperating hook processes on one local Linux workspace, same fallback slug and timestamp, durable files, provenance, exclusive kernel publication. Independent late writer first creating a target is outside this successful two-reset observation.",
  "method": "Separate Node processes with network disabled. Seed two real SQLite session transcripts with differing text and send real internal command:reset events. Pause the left actor after fs.promises.access actually failed with ENOENT but before returning that identical error to the hook. Start the right actor before releasing the left. Release only after the right actor actually completed the baseline write, or strace proved the authentic newer lock rejected simultaneous acquisition with EEXIST. Production name allocation, provenance and file publication are unmodified.",
